   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "q",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "STAFF HEARING SURVEY — SEPT/OCT 1998 (Lind)\n\n31 of 40 staff report tinnitus since Run 7.\n22 report hearing their own voice when alone. Always their own voice. Always saying something they have already said.\n9 report it answering them.\n\nNo one reports it when they work in pairs.\n\nRecommendation: nobody works alone. Nobody listens alone. Hale has agreed. The Director has not.",
    "title": "Staff hearing survey"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "s",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "Okafor, T. Signals supervisor. 44.\n\nPresents: persistent tinnitus, insomnia. States he hears his own voice in the walls 'saying things I said last week. Things I said on the radio.'\n\nI asked him if it ever says anything new.\n\nHe said: 'Not yet.'\n\nPrescribed: rest. Earplugs. Two people in the room at all times.\n— S.L.",
    "title": "Treatment log — Okafor, T."
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
  {
   "symbol": "t",
   "kind": "note",
   "props": {
    "text": "To whoever has the morgue tonight:\n\nThe service lift's fuse blew again (third time). Spares are in the morgue stores, top shelf.\n\nThe morgue door's pneumatics are shot. It will NOT stay open on its own. Put something heavy on the treadle plate outside it or you'll be shut in with the drawers until morning, and I am not coming to get you.\n\n— S.L.\n\nPS. Pharmacy code is changed. Ask me. Do NOT write it on the wall again, Brandt.",
    "title": "Memo — S. Lind"
   },
   "sequence": -1,
   "lines": -1
  },
